        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-25T09:39:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand `current_level` will be reset to 0 eventually, but they will be used from the different places.\n\n`charger_profile_override` is called in the `charger_task`, and `current_update` is called in the `hook_task`.  Those function calls could be interleaved, and preempted. So, there\u0027s a chance that the current_level is -1 and will be touched by charger_task hence caused underflow.\n\nIt\u0027s fixed now by line:77\u0027s guard, and you could drop \n\n```\n\tif (current_level \u003c 0)\n\t\tcurrent_level \u003d 0;\n```.",
      "parentUuid": "25727c62_0101b1f6",
      "range": {
